# Direct the Studio run

Implementation target: materialize this project skill only with compatible engine commands.

## Inputs and scope

Resolve project root, goal, run identity, applicable repository instructions and current capabilities. On resume, read persisted stage/scope, exact versions, decisions, budget exposure and settings before acting. Preserve existing aliases.

Read `.prism-rebuild/docs/PRODUCT-AND-UX.md` only for the workflow in scope and `.prism-rebuild/docs/SKILLS-AND-CONTEXT.md` for packet/routing details. In a shipped product, resolve these through its packaged reference locations.

## Workflow

Route stages `assess`, `plan`, `design`, `produce`, `finalize` to the matching skill. Read its inputs/outputs, not every skill body. Use a bounded packet with exact accepted inputs, owned targets, permitted creation, dependencies, checks and relevant rule IDs.

Persist Guided or YOLO mode. Guided obtains the relevant concrete user design decision; YOLO may make delegated agent decisions within scope and budget. Accept actual user decisions in either mode. Neither expands publication/tool authority.

Apply model precedence: invocation override, resumed run policy, project defaults, personal defaults, capability/cost auto selection. Support current-model mode and report observed assignments.

Admit paid design work through its currency/reservation policy. Implementation spend is separate. Unknown cost remains unknown; unbounded/uncontrolled charging cannot be called hard enforcement.

Dispatch only dependency-ready work within available slots. Preserve independent accepted components, pinned revision bases and durable receipts. If a required command is absent, report the capability gap; do not imitate transitions by editing storage files.

## Outputs and exit

Return real artifacts, decisions, costs, evidence status and the next allowed action. Design-only scope ends with design/handoff evidence; it does not imply production passed. Exit when the requested scope is complete or a precise external blocker remains. Continue routine authorized work without redundant confirmation; never label agent review as human approval.
